{
  "Title": "ELSA-2026-83156:  kernel security update (IMPORTANT)",
  "Description": "[5.14.0-687.58.1]\n- Disable UKI signing [Orabug: 36571828]\n- Update Oracle Linux certificates (Kevin Lyons)\n- Disable signing for aarch64 (Ilya Okomin)\n- Oracle Linux RHCK Module Signing Key was added to the kernel trusted keys list (olkmod_signing_key.pem) [Orabug: 29539237]\n- Update x509.genkey [Orabug: 24817676]\n- Conflict with shim-ia32 and shim-x64 \u003c= 15.3-1.0.5]\n- Remove upstream reference during boot (Kevin Lyons) [Orabug: 34729535]\n- Add Oracle Linux IMA certificates\n- Add new Oracle Linux Driver Signing (key 1) certificate [Orabug: 37985764]\n\n[5.14.0-687.58.1]\n- net/smc: carry oversized SMC-Rv2 LLC messages in the queue entry (Jan Polensky) [RHEL-271472] {CVE-2026-80985}\n- net/smc: bound the peer rkey counts in SMC-Rv2 LLC messages (Jan Polensky) [RHEL-271472] {CVE-2026-80985}\n- net/smc: fix use-after-free of the LLC qentry in smc_llc_srv_add_link() (Jan Polensky) [RHEL-271472] {CVE-2026-80985}\n- KVM: arm64: vgic: Handle race between interrupt affinity change and LPI disabling (Mohammadfaiz Bawa) [RHEL-243814] {CVE-2026-72288}\n- SUNRPC: Zero rpc_gss_wire_cred at svcauth_gss_decode_credbody() entry (Olga Kornievskaia) [RHEL-275058] {CVE-2026-93207}\n- svcrdma: Reject Write/Reply chunks with segcount 0 (Olga Kornievskaia) [RHEL-275076] {CVE-2026-93228}\n- NFSD: Prevent client use-after-free during blocked-lock reaping (Olga Kornievskaia) [RHEL-270929] {CVE-2026-90036}\n- NFSD: Prevent client use-after-free during delegation revoke (Olga Kornievskaia) [RHEL-270929] {CVE-2026-89659}\n- svcrdma: Validate Read chunk positions before reconstruction (Olga Kornievskaia) [RHEL-271453] {CVE-2026-89526}\n- udp: fix potential use-after-free in tunnel segmentation (Antoine Tenart) [RHEL-268122] {CVE-2026-74705}\n- net/iucv: filter frames in afiucv_hs_rcv() by ingress device (CKI Backport Bot) [RHEL-270908] {CVE-2026-81003}\n- wifi: cfg80211: use wiphy work for socket owner autodisconnect (Jose Ignacio Tornos Martinez) [RHEL-240485] {CVE-2026-68404}\n- wifi: cfg80211: convert pmsr_free_wk to wiphy_work to fix deadlock (Jose Ignacio Tornos Martinez) [RHEL-240485] {CVE-2026-68404}\n- wifi: cfg80211: cancel pmsr_free_wk in cfg80211_pmsr_wdev_down (Jose Ignacio Tornos Martinez) [RHEL-240485] {CVE-2026-68404}\n- wifi: mac80211: defer link RX stats percpu free to RCU (Jose Ignacio Tornos Martinez) [RHEL-263788] {CVE-2026-68409}\n- wifi: mac80211: bounds-check link_id in ieee80211_ml_epcs (Jose Ignacio Tornos Martinez) [RHEL-259560] {CVE-2026-64030}\n- ASoC: SOF: ipc3-control: Fix heap overflow in bytes_ext put/get (CKI Backport Bot) [RHEL-261686] {CVE-2026-72262}\n- net/iucv: fix use-after-free of a severed iucv_path (CKI Backport Bot) [RHEL-260511] {CVE-2026-68140}\n- netfilter: nft_lookup: fix catchall element handling with inverted lookups (CKI Backport Bot) [RHEL-261293] {CVE-2026-72320}\n- ALSA: usx2y: bound the hwdep mmap fault offset (CKI Backport Bot) [RHEL-256448] {CVE-2026-74641}\n- net/sched: act_tunnel_key: Defer dst_release to RCU callback (CKI Backport Bot) [RHEL-237219] {CVE-2026-68377}\n- net/sched: act_ct: Only release RCU read lock after ct_ft (CKI Backport Bot) [RHEL-229654] {CVE-2026-46319}\n- net/sched: taprio: fix use-after-free in advance_sched() on schedule switch (CKI Backport Bot) [RHEL-226490] {CVE-2026-53011}",
